[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to a Path Traversal vulnerability. This vulnerability occurs because the code constructs file paths by directly concatenating user-supplied input from the tar archive entries with the destination path without properly sanitizing or validating these inputs. If an archive entry contains relative paths such as "../", it could allow writing files outside the intended destination directory, leading to potential overwriting of arbitrary files on the system. This vulnerability is exploited when extracting maliciously crafted tar archives that include such traversal sequences in their file paths.

